A||N||2||Seanh||Oh no, not another cooling problem! Need Quick Help||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||04-27-2001||10:39 PM||||Well, the car has been running fine, and normal temerature. Today, I drove it into the grage, left it and came out about 1.5-2 hours later to open the grage door and I noticed a coolant puddle behind the car. I checked, and it originated under the puke tank side/area of the radiator. I didn't see any coolant dripping, but I did see some signs of coolant along the bottem edge of where the radiator fan part bolts to the radiator. I looked in the puke tank, suspecting it was leaking and the level was very low. I filled it up, and started the car. The car got up to normal temerature (about 170-180), and stayed right there when the thermostate opened. No coolant was comming out either. Whats going on? I am afraid to take it out on the town tonight for fear it might overheat or somthing. Should I go ahead and take it out tonight? I guess it would be better to have it cause problems tonight then tomarrow on my way to work. What should I do?<P>Also, how long should I wait to remove the thermostat cap or radiator cap? Manual says 3 hours, but I can't wait that long if I could possibly avoid it. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-27-2001||10:47 PM||||you can remove it as soon as the system cools. If that takes 1 hour or three then that's what it takes. My rule is that if you can lay your hand on the engine then it's cool enough to at least no burn the hell out of you if it sprays.<P>You need to check what cap is on the radiator. read my cooling articles. They tell you what Stant caps work. (look down for link.)<P>Assuming the car is running ok.... a common thing is for it to develop an air seep someplace. This will let allot of air in but not let out enough coolant to see it. If you have the "vented" cap on the radiator then the coolant will drain into the tank, and onto the floor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||04-27-2001||10:51 PM||||The cap just says: "Do not open hot!" and "15lbs. Closed System" Is this the right cap?||||reg||1
